    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d80">

                <pb facs="0099" n="87" xml:id="pg87"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">860M.01 Memel/577: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in Lithuania</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Norem</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Kaunas</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1939-03-22T10:00:00+01:00">March 22, 1939—10
                            a.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received 10:10 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>10. Lithuanian Foreign Minister<anchor n="48" xml:id="d80-f1"/> returned Tuesday
                    with Ger man unwritten ultimatum regarding the voluntary surrender of Memel
                    territory within 60 days. According to the plan, Lithuania will receive use of
                    port.</p>
                <p>While accepting the ultimatum in principle, the Lithuanian Government is
                    employing the method of appeal to the signatory powers.<anchor n="49"
                        xml:id="d80-f2"/> The orderly transfer of the territory this week is
                    foreseen. The Germans are preparing for a triumphal entry. The treatment of the
                    Lithuanian Minister for Foreign Affairs in Berlin was typically German—brutal
                    and discourteous. Slight disturbances noted in country.</p>
                <p>A delegation, most likely headed by Minister for Foreign Affairs, will leave for
                    Berlin tonight to discuss methods of transfer and other questions involved.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Norem</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d80-f1" n="48" xml:id="d80-f1-content">
